{"id": "EUVD-2026-81967", "enisaUuid": "16b0fdcd-a9d0-3073-a9f3-449d20a338ee", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nARM: 9481/2: breakpoint: CFI breakpoints only on demand\n\nThis removes the stub hw_breakpoint_cfi_handler() from ARM, making\nit not steal breakpoint type 0x03 (ARM_ENTRY_CFI_BREAKPOINT) unless\nCFI is actively used in the kernel.\n\nWhen not instrumenting with CFI, or when a breakpoint is issued in\nuserspace, we fall through to return 1 from hw_breakpoint_pending()\n\"unhandled fault\" so userspace can make use of this breakpoint.\n\nTested with LKDTM and this command line:\necho CFI_FORWARD_PROTO > /sys/kernel/debug/provoke-crash/DIRECT\nstill works as expected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:24", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/314f1a6762b5d51b37784ed7dc701d4c3d893703", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da64b150e4b7bee615b33ab21f3137c31ec36922", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ed9bff906cf8036531d1559f10e82733a52b41f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-83wp-8ph8-8m42", "CVE-2026-90306"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b51aa43-7864-3dd2-8f0c-663ba5237e96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "3fc266c0-ce8d-3393-95e0-be836edade83", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "5373114d-5558-33ee-845f-a0b6f70fb8b7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "53818cc3-0dd8-3622-9748-e03b301ce665", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c3f89986fde7bb9ccc86a901bf28e1f7d69fc3b3 <8ed9bff906cf8036531d1559f10e82733a52b41f"}, {"id": "84b59d6c-c524-37b8-8344-9023e52084d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c3f89986fde7bb9ccc86a901bf28e1f7d69fc3b3 <da64b150e4b7bee615b